{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1103877-need-help-preping-for-a-game","id":1103877,"title":"Need help preping for a game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-15T12:20:23-07:00","id":1103877,"title":"Need help preping for a game.","content":"I'm in the prosess of preparing for a game in which the players will be trying to take over a large town/small city at the command of their sire.<br /> The town has been home to a large brood of Duchagne (B:tC) for a very long time and they are quite used to being the only game in town however recently a number of Oberlochs (B:tH) have been forced to seek shelter there due to Werewolf activity and tensions have been rising, naturaly the players will be a small band of Mekhet embraced by an overly optimistic normad Dragon who has to make frequent appearances outside town to prevent suspicion (nobody likes being upstaged by an NPC right?) hoping to sweep in at the end and finish of the survivors after fanning the flames to encourage them to do most of the work without being found out. At present I plan on giving the Duchagne obfuscate and making Licencieux with devotions.<br /> I'm looking for advise on how to go about mapping the city (you know at some point they're going to ask so I want to be ready in advance) and any advice from people who have run similar games or otherwise have useful insights. Serve me well and I will reward you with an Actual Play of the game when it happens (subject to the game happening, me managing to write it up ect) to express my gratitude.<br /> Basically any and all help appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T14:01:21-07:00","id":1103914,"title":"","content":"Oftimes I usually look at strategy guides or other maps for video games. It's usually more appropriate for city-wide games, but things like Silent Hill and other wilderness or small-town games can fit the setting you're going for. Unclear on how big the place is.<br /> <br /> An obvious other route to go is to find an appropriately sized real-life location and maps of it via google or something.<br /> <br /> As for general game advice, this is probably also obvious but dividing up the Oberlochs and Duchagne so that there's different factions within you can deal with is a good way to go. That way, also, if the players encounter and piss off one there's reason for that vampire to not alert the entire bloodline and for them to not react appropriately.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel clanbook has an awesome Oberloch encounter in it that could add some spice and danger to that part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T15:06:38-07:00","id":1103965,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I hadn't considered game maps. I'm not certain how big a place I need at the moment but I want the players to be out numbered by more powerful vampires with just one of the factions. I'm starting them off with only 2 dots in disciplines but they'll be getting Animalism from homebrew bloodline, weakness will be if they fail on a roll to acquire knowledge they get the Obsessive condition for a number of nights equal to their Blood Potency but I'm still trying to word it so it doesn't activate on throw away roll to see if you know something rolls. At the moment I'm inclined to have only extended actions and rolls that use willpower trigger it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T08:54:07-07:00","id":1132641,"title":"","content":"My current game is coming to an end soon so I should be running within a month, I've decided on a bloodline boon for the Oberlochs (their Humanity counts as one higher for each member of the bloodline with them, this should offset the low humanity they would end up with doing what they do) but not for the Duchagne.<br /> For the players' bloodline I have everything but the wording of their boon and bane (the bloodline members suffer an obsession with knowledge, I don't want players afraid to make academics/occult rolls so at the moment I'm thinking either only extended actions and rolls that use willpower give the obsessed condition or tying it into Frenzy which is more vampire and very Mekhet but could be easily exploited to resolve the Tempted condition, for their boon I want to give them a bonus on such rolls possibly based on Blood Potency either by letting them buy extra successes at one per Vitae or allowing them to spend a Vitae when they spend Willpower to increase the number of extra dice by their BP) and a name for the bloodline although I have settled on Knowledge Seekers as their nickname in the English speaking world.<br /> Their history in brief is their founder was a scholar who made a deal with the Afhal Usum (page 78 of Skinchangers) and when one dies a Spirit with a rank equal to the Blood Potency of the Vampire emerges, this sprit is the reason for their boon and bane and takes all the vampires knowledge with it to its choir but modern members of the bloodline are unaware of this, as I intend for this bloodline to have its origin way back in Egypt I was thinking of using something from that era as the basis for their name the way Khaibit means shadow but I'm not sure of my ability to research an ancient language without doing something silly so if anyone knows a convenient site to reference it would help a lot along with advice on how to balance the boon/bane thing, as second edition seems to be trying to avoid overly harsh bloodline weaknesses I think what I've come up with should be ok I just need to decide on how to implement them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 08-22-2017, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}